{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"final"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PassthroughSubject"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Sendable"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Subscribing","type":"heading","text":"Subscribing","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A consumer subscribes when its iterator is created, which is when a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for try await"},{"type":"text","text":" loop over the subject"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(or over an operator chain built on it) begins. From then on, every value sent is buffered for that consumer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"until it is consumed, so a consumer that is slower than the sender still sees every value, in order."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Values sent while there are no subscribers are discarded; they are never replayed to a later consumer."}]},{"style":"important","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Starting a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" that iterates the subject does not mean it has subscribed yet. If values must"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not be missed, wait until the consumer has subscribed before sending, for example with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"handleEvents(receiveMakeIterator:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"name":"Important"},{"anchor":"Example","type":"heading","tex